>
  
  <!-- Alfa Laval MOPX-207 Diesel Centrifuge Skid -->
  <figure class="not-prose">
    <img
      src="/images/alfa-laval-mopx-207-centrifuge/Alfa-Laval-MOPX-207-Diesel-Centrifuge-Skid-500.webp"
      alt="Alfa Laval MOPX 207 Diesel Centrifuge Skid"
      width="500"
      height="500"
      loading="lazy"
      class="img-cap-400"
    />
    <figcaption>Alfa Laval MOPX-207 Diesel Centrifuge Skid</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <!-- MOPX 207 Operation -->
  <h2 id="operation">Operation</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href="https://www.alfalaval.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Alfa Laval</a> MOPX 207 Centrifuge is a self-cleaning, <a href="/disc-stack-centrifuge/">disc-stack centrifuge</a> ideal for the continuous, three-phase separation of fuels and mineral oils.
  </p>
  <p>
    With a <strong>7.5 HP motor</strong>, the MOPX 207 centrifuge has a bowl speed of <strong>6,325 RPM</strong>. Its OEM application table lists <strong>7,400 L/h (32.58 US GPM derived) for gas oil at 40&deg;C</strong> and <strong>5,000 L/h (22.01 US GPM derived) for diesel at 40&deg;C and 13 cSt</strong>.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Alfa Laval MOPX-207 is a versatile, 'self-cleaning' centrifuge that is small enough to be manually serviced without the need for lifting devices (cranes, hoists, etc.)
  </p>
  <p>
    Capacity is fluid- and condition-specific; the gas-oil value must not be reused as a diesel, condensate, waste-oil, or water capacity. See Dolphin's <a href="/technical-data/">technical-data methodology and machine-readable registry</a> for the source basis and conversion method.
  </p>

  <p>
    Dolphin Centrifuge is the independent specialist in Alfa Laval centrifuges. Apart from Alfa Laval itself, Dolphin is the reliable source for quality Alfa Laval machines: remanufactured MOPX 207 centrifuges, turnkey systems, parts, and service, built on 40+ years of Alfa Laval experience and led by Sanjay Prabhu, M.S.M.E. Dolphin is an independent remanufacturer and is not affiliated with or authorized by Alfa Laval.
  </p>

  <p>
    The MOPX 207 is supplied either as a bare remanufactured centrifuge or as the Dolphin <a href="/centrifuges/dmpx-028/">DMPX-028 module</a>, a Dolphin-engineered turnkey skid featuring a remanufactured Alfa Laval MOPX 207. WHPX 407 is a separate base-machine option for that commercial module and retains its own capacity records. The hero photo above is a DMPX-028 module running a MOPX 207 at a power plant.
  </p>

  <figure class="not-prose">
    <img
      src="/images/alfa-laval-mopx-207-centrifuge/Alfa-Laval-MOPX207-Used-Oil-Centrifuge-500.webp"
      alt="Alfa Laval MOPX 207 Used Oil Centrifuge"
      width="500"
      height="500"
      loading="lazy"
      class="img-cap-400"
    />
    <figcaption>Alfa Laval MOPX 207 Used Oil Centrifuge</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <!-- MOPX Applications -->
  <h2 id="applications-mopx">Applications</h2>
  <p>
    The MOPX-207 finds a variety of applications in fuel and lubrication purification applications. Some of the popular applications are:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/alfa-laval-diesel-centrifuge/">Diesel Fuel</a></li>
    <li><a href="/waste-oil-centrifuge/">Waste Oil</a></li>
    <li><a href="/black-diesel-centrifuge/">Black Diesel</a></li>
    <li><a href="/wvo-centrifuge-separator/">WVO or Yellow Grease</a></li>
    <li><a href="/biodiesel-centrifuge/">Biodiesel Glycerol</a></li>
    <li><a href="/fuel-oil-centrifuge/">Heavy Fuel Oil</a></li>
    <li><a href="/machine-coolant-centrifuge/">Machining Coolant</a></li>
    <li><a href="/quench-oil-centrifuge/">Quenching Oil</a></li>
    <li><a href="/crude-oil-centrifuge/">Light Crude Oil</a></li>
  </ul>

  <figure class="not-prose">
    <img
      src="/images/alfa-laval-mopx-207-centrifuge/Alfa-Laval-Explosion-Proof-Centrifuge-500.webp"
      alt="Alfa Laval MOPX 207 Explosion Proof Centrifuge"
      width="500"
      height="500"
      loading="lazy"
      class="img-cap-400"
    />
    <figcaption>Alfa Laval MOPX-207 Explosion Proof Centrifuge</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <!-- MOPX Specifications -->
  <h2 id="specifications-mopx">Specifications</h2>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto not-prose">
    <table class="w-full text-sm text-text border-collapse">
      <thead>
        <tr class="bg-navy text-white">
          <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold w-1/2">Parameter</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Value</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 hover:bg-gray-50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Centrifuge Model</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono">Alfa Laval MOPX 207 TGT</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 hover:bg-gray-50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">OEM Application Capacity - Gas Oil</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono">7,400 L/h (32.58 US GPM derived), 40 &deg;C</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 hover:bg-gray-50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">OEM Application Capacity - Diesel</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono">5,000 L/h (22.01 US GPM derived), 40 &deg;C, 13 cSt</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 hover:bg-gray-50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">OEM Application Capacity - R&amp;O / Engine Lube Oil</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono">2,600 L/h (11.45 US GPM derived), 80&ndash;90 &deg;C</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 hover:bg-gray-50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">OEM Application Capacity - Steam Turbine Lube Oil</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono">4,800 L/h (21.13 US GPM derived), 60&ndash;70 &deg;C</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 hover:bg-gray-50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Sludge Space</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono">1.00 Gallons</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 hover:bg-gray-50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Bowl Speed</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono">6,325 RPM</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 hover:bg-gray-50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Net Weight</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono">1,800 Lbs.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 hover:bg-gray-50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Dimensions</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono">30" x 38" x 43" (Bare Centrifuge)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 hover:bg-gray-50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Motor Power</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono">7.5 HP</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Voltages</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono">230 / 460 V; 3-Phase</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Capacities retain the published L/h values; US GPM is derived using L/h &divide; 227.124707 and shown to two decimal places. See the <a href="/technical-data/">authoritative technical-data registry</a>.</p>

  <div class="bg-gold/10 border-l-4 border-gold rounded-r-xl p-5 my-8 not-prose">
    <p class="font-bold text-navy text-base mb-1">Need the complete datasheet?</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-text-light leading-relaxed mb-4">We'll email the complete datasheet - usually within one business day.</p>
    <a href="/contact-for-alfa-laval-centrifuges/" class="inline-block bg-gold text-navy font-semibold px-5 py-2 rounded-lg hover:bg-gold/90 transition-colors text-sm">Request the full spec sheet (PDF) -></a>
  </div>

  <!-- Material of Construction -->
  <h3 id="material">Material of Construction</h3>
  <p>
    The Alfa Laval MOPX 207 is designed for mineral oil and fuel separation applications. Therefore, the material used in its construction is well suited for such uses. The following table lists the various components of the centrifuge and the material it is made of.
  </p>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto not-prose">
    <table class="w-full text-sm text-text border-collapse">
      <thead>
        <tr class="bg-navy text-white">
          <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold w-1/2">Component</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-3 text-left font-semibold">Material</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 hover:bg-gray-50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3">Bowl Body &amp; Bowl Hood</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono">316L Duplex Stainless Steel</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 hover:bg-gray-50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3">Disc Stack</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono">316L Duplex Stainless Steel</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 hover:bg-gray-50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3">Distributor or Disc Carrier</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono">Marine Grade Bronze or 316 Stainless Steel (Special Order)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 hover:bg-gray-50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3">Top Disc</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono">Marine Grade Bronze or 316 Stainless Steel (Special Order)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 hover:bg-gray-50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3">Top Covers (Collecting)</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono">Silium (Aluminum Alloy)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="hover:bg-gray-50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3">Frame</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono">Nodular Cast Iron</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <InstallationRequirements />

  <!-- WHPX 407 Section -->
  <h2 id="whpx-407">Alfa Laval WHPX 407 Partial-Discharge Disc-Stack Centrifuge</h2>
  <p>
    The Alfa Laval WHPX 407 Centrifuge is a self-cleaning disc-stack centrifuge designed for the three-phase separation of fuel oils, such as <a href="/fuel-oil-centrifuge/">light fuel oil</a> (LFO).
  </p>
  <p>
    With a <strong>10 HP motor</strong>, the WHPX 407 centrifuge has a bowl speed of <strong>7,125 RPM</strong>. Its OEM application table lists <strong>6,000 L/h (26.42 US GPM derived) for marine diesel</strong> and <strong>2,800 L/h (12.33 US GPM derived) for 180 cSt HFO</strong>, centrifuged at 90&ndash;98&deg;C. These are separate fluid records, not one universal WHPX 407 rating.
  </p>
  <p>
    Also, the WHPX-407 is a <strong>partial-discharge centrifuge</strong>. This means that this centrifuge is capable of discharging only the accumulated sludge and minimizing <a href="/centrifuge-product-loss-during-discharge/">fluid loss</a>.
  </p>

  <figure class="not-prose">
    <img
      src="/images/alfa-laval-mopx-207-centrifuge/Alfa_Laval_MOPX-207_Centrifuge_Module_by_Dolphin_Centrifuge-500.webp"
      alt="Alfa Laval MOPX 207 Centrifuge Module by Dolphin Centrifuge"
      width="500"
      height="500"
      loading="lazy"
      class="img-cap-400"
    />
    <figcaption>Alfa Laval MOPX 207 Centrifuge Module by Dolphin Centrifuge</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h2 id="applications-whpx">Applications</h2>
  <p>
    Similar to the Alfa Laval MOPX-207, the WHPX-407 finds many applications in all kinds of 3-phase separation duties. Some of the popular applications are:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/fuel-oil-centrifuge/">Light Fuel Oil</a></li>
    <li><a href="/machine-coolant-centrifuge/">Machining Coolant</a></li>
    <li><a href="/quench-oil-centrifuge/">Quench Oil</a></li>
    <li><a href="/cutting-oil-centrifuge/">Cutting Oil</a></li>
    <li><a href="/cutting-oil-centrifuge/#draw-oil">Draw Oil</a></li>
  </ul>

