  <!-- MOPX 207 vs WHPX 407 -->
  <h3 id="mopx-vs-whpx">Alfa Laval MOPX 207 vs WHPX 407</h3>
  <p>
    Both machines are Alfa Laval self-cleaning, three-phase disc-stack centrifuges in the same frame size, and Dolphin supplies and remanufactures both. The practical differences are the discharge type and the drive:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Alfa Laval MOPX 207:</strong> full-discharge bowl, 6,325 RPM, 7.5 HP, 1.00 gallon sludge space, and an OEM diesel application value of 5,000 L/h (22.01 US GPM derived) at 40 &deg;C and 13 cSt. The whole bowl content is ejected on each shot, which suits heavier or stickier solids.</li>
    <li><strong>Alfa Laval WHPX 407:</strong> partial-discharge bowl, 7,125 RPM, 10 HP, 1.30 gallon sludge space, an OEM marine-diesel value of 6,000 L/h (26.42 US GPM derived) at 40 &deg;C and 13 cSt, and separate HFO and lube-oil records. Only the accumulated sludge is ejected, which keeps <a href="/centrifuge-product-loss-during-discharge/">product loss</a> low on valuable fluids.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Dolphin's <a href="/centrifuges/dmpx-028/">DMPX-028 module</a> is built on either base machine, so the choice comes down to fluid value, solids character, and which remanufactured Alfa Laval bowl is in stock.
  </p>

  <!-- WSPX 207 Section -->
  <h2 id="wspx-207">Alfa Laval WSPX 207 TGP Partial-Discharge <a href="/disc-stack-centrifuge/">Disc-Stack Centrifuge</a></h2>
  <p>
    The Alfa Laval WSPX 207 Centrifuge is a self-cleaning disc-stack centrifuge designed for the three-phase concentration of water-based liquids such as machine coolants and washer liquids.
  </p>
  <p>
    The WSPX 207 has a 7.5 HP motor and a 6,400 RPM bowl. Dolphin publishes a separate 20 US GPM application figure for water-based machining coolant; it is not a MOPX 207 or WHPX 407 OEM capacity and is outside the current OEM capacity registry.
  </p>

